A||N||4||Shunyata||An introduction, and a ramble.||||6||
Z||000000||Shunyata||01-10-2001||03:09 AM||||'lo peoples. i've been browsing through the archives the last week or so, finally got around to registering. i live in san luis obispo county, california. own a 86 GT, auto, sucks up what little money i have, but i love the thing. got it in november '00, put a little over 4000 miles on it so far, not quite sure how, seeing as every two weeks or so it's on jackstands in my driveway. i drive it really hard, and im sure that doesnt help any, but its damn fun. never worked on a car before i got it, slowly learning with each breakdown. as i said, this is gonna be a ramble, so how about a little history of the car? as soon as i brought it home, steam started coming from the front end, one of the little black tanks on the side of the radiator cracked, pulled it out, got it fixed. next to go was the heater core... shortly after that i was erm... 'cruising' with a friend, following his honda down the freeway at 95, someone going about 55 came on the freeway, immediatly moved over into the fast lane, cut him off... we both slammed on our brakes, my back end slid out, and i flew into the guard rail  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> my driving skills are... well, close to non-existant, so obviously i had no business going over 65. that slowed me down a bit. $100 in parts from the salvage yard and an alignment and it was back on the road... still needs some body panels and a paintjob sometime down the road when i can afford it. about a week and a half ago it died while i was getting on the freeway, wouldnt start again, got it towed to my house, thought i had blown the engine or some other godawful thing, but the engine was turning over fine, just wouldnt start... a friend came over and we started tinkering with it, he started checking connections and found a plug that wasnt seated all the way, pushed it in, and all is lovely again.<BR>i cant decide if i want to work on bringing it as close as i can to looking like it just drove off a new car lot, or give it a new 'personality'.<BR>i've only met one other fiero owner so far, he had a white gt, was working at a gas station i pulled into one night...<BR>i dont know how much i'll be able to contribute to this forum since my knowledge is so limited, but i'll do what i can. from the outside looking in, it seems like a spiffy place here.<P><P>------------------<BR>-Shun<BR>86.5 GT||||reg||6
Z||000001||tgowens||01-10-2001||04:59 AM||||first of all, welcome to the Forum - here you will find out everything you ever want to know (and even some things you may not care to know) about the Fiero,,,,,,<P>Let me also say that, even though I work in Richmond, CA (right above Oakland in the East Bay) at the Fiero Shop (we can help you in any way with advice or parts to repair or restore your Fiero) - I am in Paso Robles every weekemd and not far from you.......,aybe we could meet sometime on a weekend and I could share some thoughts with you. In the meantime, if you want a little history on my car (to let you know what you are in for! - just kidding) - take a look at my web site --  <A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||01-10-2001||05:10 AM||||Not completely sure where San Luis is exactly but this Saturday, the San Diego Fiero Club is having a car show. Fieros West is getting some people together to trave down there saturday morning from Orange County. If you can get down there you will probably have more ideas than you know what to do with!<P>Sounds like you want to first get your Fiero dependable before you think about making it your own. If you are having problems with overheating it might be time for you to learn about the waterpump! <P>Good luck to you and welcome!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000003||2xsess||01-10-2001||05:20 AM||||Welcome to the forum  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>As you'll soon see a lot of us ramble every now and then. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Shunyata||01-10-2001||05:49 AM||||thank you all, for the welcome =)<P>tgowens- i'd definitly be up for meeting sometime, e-mail me at didnos@hotmail.com (i rarely check the email account i used to register, they wouldnt let me register with a hotmail address) or icq me sometime when you'll be in the area and have some free time and be up for it and such.<P>WKD- i'd love to head down there, but i work weekend evenings, and right now i dont trust my car enough to take it that far from home. someday, when im comfortable with it and theres another show, and im not so broke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>and overheating- that was mainly just a problem the first day. when i drained it and pulled the radiator out i found my coolant was, well, water.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> im not quite sure how that happened. took care of that, for a while had a slight problem if i was sitting at a stoplight or in traffic for too long, but someone on here in the archives mentioned something about hitting the 'norm' button to turn the fan on, tried that the other day, worked, and doesnt seem to be a problem now. learning about the water pump now wouldnt be a bad thing to do though, im sure i'll need the knowledge later.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>and i seem to ramble more than most people, makes up for how little i talk in real life =)<P><P>------------------<BR>-Shun<BR>86.5 GT||||reg||1
